Z||000000||Bluemagic||12-18-2001||10:32 AM||||Ilearn so much from you guys that I had to provoke  your genius minds,<BR> Do you think Aids is a man made disease that went wrong like Anthrax and how comeit wasn't around in the 60's and 70's let me know your thoughts.<P>------------------<BR>Keith<BR>85 SE Fiero 4.9L Caddy <BR>345hp||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||12-18-2001||10:39 AM||||AIDS has been around for a very long time, just not in humans.  It's been a simian (ape) disease long before humans contracted it.  Apparently there was an incident where a human or humans contracted the disease from apes, and it's spread since then.  There was research into a "Patient Zero" back in the 80's, an airline Steward who was believed to have infect literally 1000's of people before his death from the disease.  Whether he did this knowingly or not is another issue.<P>I cannot verify this info, but it's what I found out when I was learning about it back in the late '80's.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||12-18-2001||10:44 AM||||one of my college profs did a lot of AIDS research in the 80s at John Hopkins University, she wrote many medical articles about her work.. she told us some stuff about what she had researched, but since it wasn't a medical class, she didn't go into a lot of detail.. still interesting though.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000003||JSocha||12-18-2001||11:39 AM||||I thought it went back further  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">.<P>I was watching a program on it back in the mid '90's (I think it was on Discovery, just know I had satellite) that said they were able to trace AIDS back to as early as the 1900's.  They did a test (now that the technology is available) on skeletal remains based on the disease and symptoms that were documented at that time and how they died and discovered they died of either a similar or the exact same disease we have come to know as HIV/AIDS.<P>I'm just going from memeory at this point though.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Voytek||12-18-2001||11:56 AM||||If it dates way back, then, can someone tell me, why it didn't spread in the past the way it's spreading today?<P>It's kind of a loaded question.  I'm expecting this to get into the morality debate.<P>First time I've heard about AIDS was about 1985.<P>Coincidentally, I've heard the stuard story too.  Whether it makes a difference or not, he was gay.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||RedHaze86SD4||12-18-2001||12:25 PM||||My uncle died christmas eve of '93 of aids. At the time he was the longest documented survivor having it for almost ten years. Yeah I know for the time ten years was pretty hard to believe. During the time he had it I helped him some with the local support groups and what not, and while doing research we traced few documented cases back to the ealry 1900's. I think it was around 1910 or 1911. A doctor in caught it in New England somewhere. Sorry Don't remember much more.. '93 was a while ago.....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RHplate.jpg">  Have to make new sig. RedHaze is now Black with a Red Haze :)||||reg||4
Z||000006||Steve Normington||12-18-2001||12:30 PM||||Anthrax isn't a man made disease. There are altered strains, but the basic form is naturally occuring.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||12-18-2001||12:35 PM||||I think the problem with aids deaths is that you don't die of the aids disease, you die of other causes that cannot be controlled because of the aids virus. Therefore many early deaths were chalked up to other causes. Until a few years ago Doctors in Zimbabwe were not allowed to put down aids as the cause of death, they had to put down the actual final cause - pneumonia, heart failure etc. Something like dying of "old age"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Mach10||12-18-2001||02:49 PM||||A few things about HIV: <P>-It's growth in the last hundred years is a pretty typical exponential growth curve. Nothing unusual. Similar to SIV, humans aren't affected by the natural form of SIV. A mutation allowed it to cross over to humans. Since then, there have been NUMEROUS mutations, including a few Super-HIV bugs that are MUCH faster, almost impossible to trace, and resistant to all the available drugs. Let's just hope that HIV doesn't learn to become Airborne<P>-It hasn't been mentioned, but HAS been implied that this disease tends towards homosexual black males. That's complete and utter B.S. You are no more likely to contract aids in gay activities than "normal" hetero activities. It just so happens that the "center" for aids infection happens to be bunch of starving 3rd world countries. E.G., no medical help, no education, hardly any condoms... Perfect little breeding ground for an STD like Aids. ||||reg||4
