Z||000010||Patrick's Dad||12-19-2001||09:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>Warondrugs/stupid-laws/religios nuts all help spread by not helping control spread by free condums in schools. and needels for junkusers on the street NO WE CAN'T DO THATERS are still at it. like instead of control of sexforsale<BR>lets pass stupid laws and jail girls and hope AIDS goes away instead of free help to give them freesshit if infected to keep them off the working streets.<BR>THATS WHY LAWS NEED TO be RATIONAL and revised offten and never gods.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Huh?<P>If I decode this right, then we should create programs to take our money and give it to:<P>1) Condom giveaways at school, which encourage children to give in to their primal urges, sending a message that it's OK to have sex, as long as you've hit puberty. Girls are, of course, good for nothing else, so, if it feels good, do it. The condom will protect both of you from disease and pregnancy...98 of the time. In fact, if the HIV virus were ¼" in diameter, a pinhole in a condom is a double door.<P>2) Hookers, who, in the normal excersize of their profession, open themselves up (literally) to hundreds of idiots who, like their high school couterparts, can't control their urges, and are willing to pay money for it. We should feed, clothe and house the ones who "accidentally" get these diseases, so the aforementioned clods don't bring them home to their wives and girlfriends. Oh, *that* will be 100% effective....<P>3) Clean needles for junkies. Oh, yeah, that's like giving more bullets to al-Qaeda (sp?). It's OK if you're taking target practice, as long as the violence won't spill over to innocents. Guess what? A druggie will do anything for a high. That's why they don't care about clean needles if they don't have one readily available. Their own life isn't worth it. No one else's would be, either, if they happened to be in the way. And you think that the dealer will say, "Oh, no, no more for you until you've calmed down."?<P>We need more rational (read, permissive) laws in this country like we need more, well, liberals. That strategy's done so well for the anti-gun lobbyists.<P>What we need is self control. As rayb put it so succinctly, we can't legislate it. We have to teach it. We have to practice it. We need to uphold it. And if we do, our legislators will finally be able to say, "See? One of our programs worked! Let's take more money from the people and give it to someone else."||||reg||1
